**IMPORTANT FUNCTIONALITY: PLAY A BEEP SOUND WHEN CLICKED.**

When a visitor clicks Call Waiter:

1. Play a short, clear, professional beep sound.
2. Play the sound once per click.
3. Use a pleasant notification tone, not a loud alarm.
4. Trigger the sound directly from the click so it works with browser audio restrictions.
5. Add a small visual click animation.
6. Open the assistance modal.

The beep must:
- Work on desktop and mobile browsers where audio is supported.
- Not play automatically when the page loads.
- Not loop continuously.
- Not play repeatedly from a single click.
- Have a reasonable volume.
- Include a mute/unmute option if appropriate.

If no external sound file is supplied, generate the short beep using the Web Audio API.

Example implementation:

```js
function playWaiterBeep() {
  const AudioContextClass =
    window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext;

  if (!AudioContextClass) return;

  const audioContext = new AudioContextClass();

  const oscillator = audioContext.createOscillator();
  const gain = audioContext.createGain();

  oscillator.type = "sine";
  oscillator.frequency.value = 880;

  gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.15, audioContext.currentTime);
  gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(
    0.001,
    audioContext.currentTime + 0.25
  );

  oscillator.connect(gain);
  gain.connect(audioContext.destination);

  oscillator.start();
  oscillator.stop(audioContext.currentTime + 0.25);
}
```

Use this function when the user clicks the Call Waiter button. Handle browser audio restrictions and cleanup appropriately.

